<urn:atm:triage:finding/RRG-GRAFT-LEASE-RESTART-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "RRG-GRAFT-LEASE-RESTART-001" ;
  triage:title "hermes-atm graft receiver registration does not survive a daemon restart on rand-m5, so nudges to hermes-harness agents stop after every daemon cycle while mailbox delivery keeps working" ;
  triage:description "Reported by fenix@rand-m5 at 20:13Z on 2026-09-03 during the 1.4.10 Colima pre-tier host check: after each daemon cycle that day (1.4.9 and 1.4.10 stage, relink, kickstart of com.atm.daemon.crosshost-smoke), atm doctor --json reports graft_receivers as an empty list, and nothing re-registers the hermes-atm receiver. Effect: mailbox delivery still works but no nudges reach hermes-harness agents; loki accumulated 77 unread including both Colima GO dispatches and never started until Rand nudged him manually. atm-dev tmux-hook nudges are a separate path and unaffected. Code reading on 0656b8a28: leases are durable rows in graft_receiver_endpoints (atm-storage-rusqlite graft_receiver_endpoint_store.rs) and the doctor report lists every roster member with a row regardless of age (atm-core doctor mod.rs graft_receivers_doctor_report), so an empty list means the row is absent, not stale. Only an owner-matched unregister deletes a row; the store refresh returns NotOwner for an absent row as well as a foreign generation (refresh changed == 0), and the receiver lease state machine in atm-graft runtime lease_client.rs then sets displaced permanently and never re-announces (RegisteredGraftReceiver::refresh). The receiver also caches its daemon client permanently after the first connect_existing (lease_client.rs line 231). Candidate mechanisms, unconfirmed: (1) the receiver process restarted around the daemon cycle (for example a hermes gateway reset), Drop unregistered the row, and the new receiver never announced successfully; (2) the daemon restart removed or relocated the row so refresh saw NotOwner and the receiver marked itself displaced for good; (3) the cached client cannot reach the restarted daemon and every refresh fails under the 30s capped backoff. Same class as the HerdrQueueWakePump never-started finding: a lifecycle gap that needs daemon-restart resilience plus a real-startup integration test with a negative proof. Discriminating evidence requested from rand-m5 without message bodies or capability values: daemon stderr log lines for graft receiver register, refresh, and unregister around the restart; loki hermes log lines from subsystem atm_graft.receiver_loop with the outcome and error code fields; the graft_receiver_endpoints rows for the hermes agents excluding the capability column; doctor --json graft_receivers and herdr_queue_pump snapshot at 20:13Z." ;
  triage:phaseId "readiness-1.4" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "graft-receiver-lifecycle" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-03T20:30:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:RRG-S2 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-03T20:13:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RRG-GRAFT-LEASE-RESTART-001/CAND-1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RRG-GRAFT-LEASE-RESTART-001/CAND-2> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RRG-GRAFT-LEASE-RESTART-001/CAND-3> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "1" .

